Queue Conditions
Queue Full Condition

In a circular queue:

(𝑟𝑒𝑎𝑟 + 1)mod
 
𝑠𝑖𝑧𝑒 = 𝑓𝑟𝑜𝑛𝑡
Meaning: If the next position of rear is equal to front, the queue is full.

In words: The queue is full when there’s no space left to insert a new element because the rear pointer is about to overlap the front pointer.

Queue Empty Condition

Condition:
𝑓𝑟𝑜𝑛𝑡= − 1 or 𝑓𝑟𝑜𝑛𝑡 = 𝑟𝑒𝑎𝑟+1
(depending on implementation)

In words: The queue is empty when there are no elements to remove, i.e., the front pointer doesn’t point to any valid element.
